# TypeScript / Next.js conventions

- Strict TypeScript. No `any`; no non-null `!` assertion without a comment explaining why it's safe.
- React Server Components by default. Add `"use client"` only when a component needs hooks, event
  handlers, or browser APIs — push it as far down the tree as possible, not at the page level.
- Mutations go through server actions (`src/server/actions/`), not client-side fetch to a route
  handler — except the routes the spec calls for explicitly: `/api/blocks/[blockId]/respond`,
  `/api/progress/heartbeat`, `/api/webhooks/*`.
- Validate all external input (server actions, route handlers) with Zod schemas shared with the
  client form, per `docs/09-security.mdx`.
- Auth: import from `auth.config.ts` in anything that runs on the Edge (middleware); import from
  `auth.ts` (which pulls in the Prisma adapter) everywhere else. Never import `auth.ts` from
  middleware.

```typescript
// BAD — untyped, no validation
export async function respondToBlock(blockId: string, payload: any) { ... }

// GOOD
const payload = ResponsePayloadSchema.parse(rawPayload);
export async function respondToBlock(blockId: string, payload: ResponsePayload) { ... }
```
